  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EPP - Building effective management and sustainable financing for the Okapi Wildlife Reserve through a Public-Private partnership - WCS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Central Africa Regional):  .USAID FY 2022 funds will be used to support the implementation of a public-private partnership agreement signed between the Wildlife Conservation Society (WCS) and the Congolese Institute for the Conservation of Nature to protect the resources of the Okapi Wildlife Reserve. This reserve hosts large blocks of intact forest and important populations of large mammals, including the okapi. The okapi are only found in the Democratic Republic of the Congo and the species is confirmed to be endangered. The primary objective of this agreement is to establish long-term management of this important protected area, leverage substantial private financial and technical resources from outside the country to build the capacity of park management at the local and national level. This activity will also build the constituency around this protected area and contribute to advancing CARPE&apos;s Strategy designed to maintain forest ecosystem functions of the Congo Basin and contribute to human well-being, which is vital to greater regional stability, a U.S. foreign policy priority...This activity will contribute to advancing the U.S. government&apos;s priorities in Central Africa designed to maintain the ecological integrity of the humid forest ecosystem of the Congo Basin, which is vital to regional stability, a U.S. foreign policy priority. It contributes to Joint Strategic Plan Strategic Objective 2.2: (Promote healthy, educated and productive populations in partner countries to drive inclusive and sustainable development, open new markets and support U.S. prosperity and security objectives) by protecting natural resources critical to long term, sustainable growth, and food and water security..</narrative>
  </description>
